FuseX
=====

FuseX is a ZX Spectrum emulator for macOS, Windows and Linux, based on Fuse.
Play Spectrum games, load tapes and snapshots, and try Spectranet/Spectranext
networking without physical hardware. It supports the original Spectrum models,
several clones, joysticks, disk interfaces and RZX recordings.

Download and install
--------------------

Download a build from https://github.com/speccytools/fusex/releases.
Expand Assets on the release page and choose the file for your platform.
Prereleases are available for testing; check the release notes before installing.
The "Source code" archives are for building, not running the app.

* macOS (12 Monterey or later, Intel and Apple silicon): open the .dmg,
  drag FuseX to Applications, eject the disk image, then launch FuseX.
* Windows (x64): run the *-setup.exe installer. For a portable installation,
  extract the Windows .zip into a folder and run fuse.exe; keep the accompanying
  files together.
* Linux (x64): install Flatpak through your distribution, then download the
  .flatpak bundle. From the folder containing it, run:

    flatpak remote-add --user --if-not-exists flathub https://dl.flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo
    flatpak install --user ./FuseX-*.flatpak
    flatpak run org.speccytools.FuseX

  Accept installation of the required runtime. You can also launch FuseX from
  your desktop's application menu. The bundle is small because Flatpak supplies
  the shared runtime separately.

To update, install a newer release over the existing installation. macOS and
Windows also offer in-app update checks; a release appears there after it has
been approved for automatic updates.

Getting started
---------------

Choose a Spectrum model in the machine settings, then open a tape (.tap/.tzx),
snapshot (.sna/.z80), or supported disk image from the File menu. Tape images
may need the machine's normal LOAD command; snapshots resume saved machine state.
Use the joystick settings to select the interface expected by your game.

Spectranext
-----------

Spectranext is a modern network cartridge for the ZX Spectrum. FuseX emulates
its networking and filesystem features, so you can try compatible software
or develop it using the Spectranext SDK without a cartridge.

Enable the interface in the peripheral settings: on macOS, select Spectranext
under Preferences -> Peripherals; on Windows/Linux, enable Spectranet in the
peripheral options. Reset the emulated machine after changing the interface.
Current builds include this support in the normal FuseX download.

For SDK development, also enable the GDB server in the debugger settings.
Setup and examples: https://docs.spectranext.net/tutorials/emulation
Hardware and project information: https://spectranext.net/

Build from source
-----------------

Clone with submodules, then follow the instructions for your platform:

    git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/speccytools/fusex.git
    cd fusex

macOS

Install Xcode and its command-line tools, plus Homebrew's build prerequisites:

    brew install autoconf automake libtool pkg-config
    make -C fusepb
    make -f Makefile.darwin fusex ARCHS="arm64 x86_64" \
      XCODEBUILD_SIGN_ARGS="CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY=- CODE_SIGN_STYLE=Manual DEVELOPMENT_TEAM="

The local app is fusepb/build/Deployment/FuseX.app. This uses ad-hoc signing;
distribution signing and notarization are separate steps. You can also open
fusepb/FuseX.xcodeproj in Xcode after building the dependencies.

Windows

Use the MSYS2 MinGW64 shell with GCC, Make, CMake, pkg-config, Perl, Autoconf,
Automake, Libtool and ZIP installed. Install NSIS if you want an installer.
The build script builds the bundled dependencies and creates the distribution:

    SKIP_APPCAST=1 bash build_win32.sh

Linux

Install a C11 compiler, Make, Autoconf, Automake, Libtool, pkg-config, Perl,
Bison, Flex and CMake, plus development packages for GTK 3, libspectrum,
libxml2, zlib and libpng. Build the bundled networking libraries first:

    ./autogen.sh
    make -C 3rdparty libssh2 MBEDTLS_BUILD_TARGET=lib MBEDTLS_MAKE_ARGS= MBEDTLS_CFLAGS=-fPIC
    ./configure --enable-sockets
    make
    ./fuse

See INSTALL for configure options. The Flatpak build manifest is
.github/builds/linux/org.speccytools.FuseX.json. Maintainer release instructions
are in .github/XCODE_CLOUD.md and hacking/releasing.md.

Help and credits
----------------

Report problems at https://github.com/speccytools/fusex/issues. Include your OS,
FuseX version, steps to reproduce, and any error message or crash report.

FuseX builds on the work of the Fuse and libspectrum contributors and the native
macOS port by Fredrick Meunier. See AUTHORS and COPYING for credits and licensing.
